---
title: "PDF Export - Customising Content"
enterprise: true
---

PDF Export uses Value Getters and, by default, [Value Formatters](./value-formatters/#formatting-for-export). Export callbacks can replace the resulting text without changing the values displayed in the grid.

## Customising Cell and Row Group Values

Use `processCellCallback` and `processRowGroupCallback` in `defaultPdfExportParams` to customise exported body cells and row groups.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const defaultPdfExportParams = {
    processCellCallback: (params) => `_${params.value ?? ''}_`,
    processRowGroupCallback: (params) => `row group: ${params.node.key ?? ''}`,
};
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="PdfExportParams" overrideSrc="pdf-export/pdf.json" names=["processRowGroupCallback", "processCellCallback"] config={"description":"See below the functions on the `PdfExportParams` interface to customise exported grid cell and row group values."} /%}

The following example adds the prefix `row group: ` to row-group values and surrounds body-cell values with underscores in the exported PDF.

{% gridExampleRunner title="PDF Export - Customising Row Groups" name="pdf-export-customising-row-groups" exampleHeight=520 /%}

## Customising Column Headers and Group Header Values

Use `processHeaderCallback` and `processGroupHeaderCallback` to customise exported column headers and column-group headers.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const defaultPdfExportParams = {
    processHeaderCallback: (params) => `header: ${params.api.getDisplayNameForColumn(params.column, null)}`,
    processGroupHeaderCallback: (params) =>
        `group header: ${params.api.getDisplayNameForColumnGroup(params.columnGroup, null)}`,
};
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="PdfExportParams" overrideSrc="pdf-export/pdf.json" names=["processGroupHeaderCallback", "processHeaderCallback"] config={"description":"See below the functions on the `PdfExportParams` interface to customise exported column group headers and headers."} /%}

The following example prefixes exported headers with `header: ` and exported group headers with `group header: `.

{% gridExampleRunner title="PDF Export - Customising Column Group Headers" name="pdf-export-customising-column-group-headers" exampleHeight=520 /%}

These callbacks return text. To style the processed result, use `processStyleCallback`; its `value` is the final exported string.
